---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — JJAY Campus Companion"
  description="What JJAY Campus Companion stores, where it comes from, who it is shared with, and how to delete it. No ads, no tracking, no selling data."
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="muted small">Effective September 6, 2026</p>

  <div class="card summary">
    <p>
      <strong>The short version:</strong> you can use the app without an account. If you make one,
      we store your CUNY email, the reviews and tags you post, and — if you join chat — your
      display name and your messages. No ads, no tracking, no selling data. Delete your account in
      the app and everything tied to it goes with it, chat included.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>An account is optional</h2>
  <p>
    You can browse everything in JJAY Campus Companion — classes, events, campus facilities, and
    professor reviews — without signing up. Anonymous browsing sends us nothing that identifies
    you.
  </p>

  <h2>Signing up requires a CUNY email</h2>
  <p>
    Creating an account requires an email address at one of these domains:
    <code>@login.cuny.edu</code>, <code>@jjay.cuny.edu</code>, or
    <code>@stu-mail.jjay.cuny.edu</code>. This keeps accounts limited to the CUNY community.
  </p>

  <h2>What we store</h2>
  <p>If you create an account, we store:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your email address.</li>
    <li>The professor reviews and tags you post.</li>
    <li>Your account preferences.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>And, if you join chat:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The display name you choose, and the date you accepted the chat rules.</li>
    <li>The messages, replies, reactions and GIFs you post.</li>
    <li>Any reports you file, and reports other people file about your messages — a report
      keeps a copy of the reported message so it can still be reviewed after the original is
      deleted.</li>
    <li>Who you have blocked, and any moderation record on your account (strikes, mutes).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    That data lives in <a href="https://supabase.com">Supabase</a>, the backend service the app is
    built on.
  </p>

  <h2>Chat</h2>
  <p>
    Chat is optional and separate from the rest of the app — you have to accept the chat rules and
    pick a display name before you can post. Your display name is shown on every message you send,
    alongside the channel’s other members. Your email address is never shown to other users.
  </p>
  <p>
    Messages are screened automatically before they post, and you can report a message or block
    another user from inside the app. Reported messages are reviewed by a person. A serious or
    repeated violation can mute your account temporarily.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else sees your data</h2>
  <p>We don’t sell or share your data. Three services process parts of it so the app can work:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="https://supabase.com">Supabase</a> — hosts the database and accounts. Everything
      described above is stored there.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://openai.com">OpenAI</a> — screens message text and display names for
      harassment, hate speech and threats before they post. Only the text is sent. Your email,
      your account id and your display name are not attached to it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://klipy.com">KLIPY</a> — powers GIF search, and only when you open the GIF
      picker. KLIPY receives what you type into GIF search, your device’s IP address, and a random
      id created on your device for that purpose. That id is deliberately not your account id, so
      your GIF searches are not linked to your account or your email.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where the app’s data comes from</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Professor statistics come from <a href="https://www.ratemyprofessors.com">RateMyProfessors</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Events and calendar data are gathered from public pages on
      <a href="https://www.jjay.cuny.edu">jjay.cuny.edu</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we don’t do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No ads.</li>
    <li>No selling or sharing your data.</li>
    <li>No tracking SDKs, no analytics, no cookies.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
  <p>
    Use <strong>Delete account</strong> in the app (in the Profile tab). It removes your account
    and everything tied to it — your email, your display name, your reviews and tags, your chat
    messages and reactions, your blocks, your moderation record, and any reports you filed or that
    were filed about your messages. Nothing is kept behind after deletion.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy or your data:
    <a href="mailto:support@jjayapp.com">support@jjayapp.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Not affiliated</h2>
  <p>
    JJAY Campus Companion is an independent student project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed
    by, or sponsored by John Jay College of Criminal Justice or The City University of New York.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the new version is posted here with an updated effective date.
  </p>
</Base>

